sources><source category="X" name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-8143616-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>8143616</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit> </patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1018520A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations> </citations> </technical-data> <parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ISHIHAMA YOSHIYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>JAPAN POLYCHEM CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIMIZU MASAFUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WATANABE AKIHIRA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHIHAMA, YOSHIYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>JAPAN POLYCHEM CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMIZU, MASAFUMI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WATANABE, AKIHIRA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ISHIHAMA YOSHIYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIMIZU MASAFUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WATANABE AKIHIRA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHIHAMA, YOSHIYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMIZU, MASAFUMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WATANABE, AKIHIRA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A process for producing an olefin polymer through olefin polymerization in the presence of a metallocene transition metal catalyst, while preventing polymer deposition on the reactor wall and preventing the generation of a sheet-form polymer, massive polymer, etc. to stably conduct the polymerization operation over long.  The process is characterized by polymerizing an olefin in the presence of [A] a metallocene transition metal catalyst and [B] an organoaluminum compound represented by the general formula R&lt;1&gt;n Al(OR&lt;2&gt;)3-n (wherein R&lt;1&gt; represents C1-20 alkyl, aryl, hydrogen, or halogeno; R&lt;2&gt; represents C1-20 alkyl or aryl; and n is a number satisfying 0&lt;/=n&lt;3) under such conditions that the temperature of the polymerizer wall, tw ( DEG C), and the polymerization temperature, tr ( DEG C), satisfy the following relationship 1: 0.5 &lt; tr-tw &lt; 10.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé relatif à l'élaboration d'un polymère oléfinique par polymérisation d'oléfine en présence de catalyseur à métal de transition métallocène. En cours de réaction, on empêche le dépôt de polymère sur la paroi du réacteur et on empêche aussi l'apparition de polymère du type feuille, massif, etc., de manière à conduire la polymérisation de manière stable sur une longue durée. Le procédé consiste à polymériser une oléfine en présence (A) d'un catalyseur à métal de transition métallocène et (B) d'un composé organoaluminique représenté par la formule générale R&lt;1&gt;n Al(OR&lt;2&gt;)3-n. Dans ladite formule, R&lt;1&gt; est alkyle C1-20, aryle, hydrogène ou halogéno; R&lt;2&gt; est alkyle C1-20, ou aryle; et n est un nombre qui obéit à la relation 0&lt;/=n&lt;3. La polymérisation s'effectue dans des conditions de température telles que la température de la paroi de la cuve de polymérisation, tw ( DEG C), et la température de polymérisation, tr ( DEG C), obéissent à la relation 1 ci-après: 0,5&lt;tr-tw&lt;10.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>